# Build context is the repository root (see server/Dockerfile), so this file
# decides what a `docker build` can even see. Two jobs:
#
#   1. Keep the context small. Without this, Docker uploads node_modules from
#      four npm projects plus every build output — hundreds of megabytes per
#      build.
#   2. Make it impossible for a secret or deployment state to end up in an
#      image layer. A layer is immutable and gets pushed to a registry, so
#      "delete it later" is not available.

# ── Never (secrets / deployment state) ──
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.deploy-state.json
scripts/backup-secrets.sh
**/secrets/

# ── Dependency trees (reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image) ──
**/node_modules

# ── Build output (the image builds its own) ──
server/dist
server/dist.previous
server/.dist-next.*
frontend/dist
frontend/dist-*
site/dist
desktop/dist
desktop/dist-*
mobile/dist
mobile/dist-*
mobile/android
mobile/ios
tools-rust/target
capacitor/android

# ── Test / tooling artifacts ──
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/test-results.bak
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
mobile/e2e-artifacts
frontend/.tmp-repro
graphify-out
.qoder-*
.vite-dev.log
*.log

# ── VCS and editor / agent state ──
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
.codex
.devin
.kilo
.kiro
.omo
.opencode
.firecrawl
.playwright-mcp
.agents
.codegraph

# ── Not needed by the API image ──
# The SPA and the marketing site are served by nginx from their own web roots.
# frontend/ is excluded wholesale rather than selectively: app.ts only touches
# frontend/dist as a local-dev fallback, and that path is not used in a
# container deployment.
frontend
site
mobile
desktop
capacitor
docs
tasks
assets
screenshot_*.png
*.md
!prompts/*.md
